{
  "title": "Solve x² − 5x + 6 = 0",
  "lang": "en",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Write equation",
      "say": "We start with the given quadratic equation.",
      "ops": [
        {
          "op": "write",
          "id": "main-title",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 60,
          "text": "Solve x² − 5x + 6 = 0",
          "size": 52
        },
        {
          "op": "write",
          "id": "eq",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 170,
          "text": "x² − 5x + 6 = 0",
          "size": 46
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Quadratic formula",
      "say": "Let's plug into the quadratic formula first.",
      "ops": [
        {
          "op": "write",
          "id": "qf-formula",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 280,
          "text": "x = (−b ± √(b² − 4ac)) / (2a)",
          "size": 40
        },
        {
          "op": "write",
          "id": "qf-params",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 370,
          "text": "a = 1,  b = −5,  c = 6",
          "size": 36
        },
        {
          "op": "write",
          "id": "qf-subst",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 440,
          "text": "x = (5 ± √(25 − 24)) / 2",
          "size": 38
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Simplify",
      "say": "The discriminant is 1, so this is easy.",
      "ops": [
        {
          "op": "write",
          "id": "qf-simp",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 510,
          "text": "x = (5 ± √1) / 2",
          "size": 38
        },
        {
          "op": "write",
          "id": "qf-further",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 570,
          "text": "x = (5 ± 1) / 2",
          "size": 38
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Switch to factoring",
      "say": "But factoring is even simpler here. Let's switch.",
      "ops": [
        {
          "op": "erase",
          "ids": ["qf-formula", "qf-params", "qf-subst", "qf-simp", "qf-further"]
        },
        {
          "op": "write",
          "id": "factor-hint",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 280,
          "text": "Find two numbers with product 6 and sum −5.",
          "size": 36,
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "op": "write",
          "id": "factor-eq",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 360,
          "text": "(x − 2)(x − 3) = 0",
          "size": 46
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Solve factors",
      "say": "Set each factor equal to zero and solve.",
      "ops": [
        {
          "op": "write",
          "id": "sol1",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 450,
          "text": "x − 2 = 0  ⇒  x = 2",
          "size": 40
        },
        {
          "op": "write",
          "id": "sol2",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 520,
          "text": "x − 3 = 0  ⇒  x = 3",
          "size": 40
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Verify",
      "say": "Check both solutions in the original equation.",
      "ops": [
        {
          "op": "write",
          "id": "verify1",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 610,
          "text": "x = 2:  4 − 10 + 6 = 0 ✓",
          "size": 36
        },
        {
          "op": "write",
          "id": "verify2",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 670,
          "text": "x = 3:  9 − 15 + 6 = 0 ✓",
          "size": 36
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "title": "Solving x² − 5x + 6 = 0",
  "lang": "en",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "The equation",
      "say": "We need to solve the quadratic equation x squared minus five x plus six equals zero.",
      "ops": [
        { "id": "eq", "x": 800, "y": 120, "text": "x² − 5x + 6 = 0", "size": 56, "anchor": "middle" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Try factoring",
      "say": "First, let's try factoring. We look for two numbers that multiply to 6 and add to −5.",
      "ops": [
        { "id": "fac1", "x": 400, "y": 260, "text": "Factor: find m, n such that", "size": 36 },
        { "id": "fac2", "x": 400, "y": 320, "text": "m · n = 6   and   m + n = −5", "size": 36 },
        { "id": "fac3", "x": 400, "y": 400, "text": "Try: −2 and −3?", "size": 36, "color": "blue" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check the factors",
      "say": "(−2)(−3) = 6 and (−2) + (−3) = −5. It works! So we can factor as (x − 2)(x − 3) = 0.",
      "ops": [
        { "id": "chk", "x": 400, "y": 480, "text": "(−2)(−3) = 6  ✓\n(−2) + (−3) = −5  ✓", "size": 36, "color": "green" },
        { "id": "facform", "x": 400, "y": 580, "text": "(x − 2)(x − 3) = 0", "size": 44, "color": "blue" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Switch to quadratic formula",
      "say": "But let's switch to a simpler, more general method midway: the quadratic formula. It always works.",
      "ops": [
        { "id": "switch", "x": 400, "y": 680, "text": "Switch to quadratic formula:", "size": 36, "color": "red" },
        { "id": "formula", "x": 400, "y": 740, "text": "x = [ −b ± √(b² − 4ac) ] / (2a)", "size": 40 }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Identify coefficients",
      "say": "Here a = 1, b = −5, and c = 6. Substitute these into the formula.",
      "ops": [
        { "id": "coef", "x": 400, "y": 820, "text": "a = 1,  b = −5,  c = 6", "size": 40 },
        { "id": "sub", "x": 400, "y": 880, "text": "x = [ 5 ± √(25 − 24) ] / 2", "size": 40, "color": "blue" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Simplify",
      "say": "The discriminant is 25 − 24 = 1, so the square root is 1. Thus x = (5 ± 1) / 2.",
      "ops": [
        { "id": "disc", "x": 400, "y": 940, "text": "Discriminant: 25 − 24 = 1", "size": 36 },
        { "id": "simp", "x": 400, "y": 1000, "text": "x = (5 ± 1) / 2", "size": 44, "color": "blue" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Two solutions",
      "say": "This gives two solutions: x = (5 + 1)/2 = 3 and x = (5 − 1)/2 = 2.",
      "ops": [
        { "id": "sol1", "x": 400, "y": 1080, "text": "x = (5 + 1)/2 = 3", "size": 40 },
