{
  "title": "Solve a Quadratic",
  "lang": "en",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Set up the equation",
      "say": "Start with the quadratic equation we need to solve.",
      "ops": [
        { "id": "title", "op": "write", "x": 80, "y": 45, "text": "Solve a Quadratic", "size": 56 },
        { "id": "eq0", "op": "write", "x": 100, "y": 140, "text": "x² − 5x + 6 = 0", "size": 48 }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "First: quadratic formula",
      "say": "Identify a, b, and c, then substitute into the quadratic formula.",
      "ops": [
        { "id": "introQF", "op": "write", "x": 100, "y": 230, "text": "First try the quadratic formula:", "size": 36 },
        { "id": "abc", "op": "write", "x": 100, "y": 290, "text": "a = 1,  b = −5,  c = 6", "size": 36 },
        { "id": "qf", "op": "write", "x": 100, "y": 350, "text": "x = (5 ± √(25 − 24)) / 2", "size": 40 }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Formula gives the roots",
      "say": "The discriminant is 1, so the formula gives x = 3 or x = 2.",
      "ops": [
        { "id": "disc", "op": "write", "x": 100, "y": 430, "text": "25 − 24 = 1, so √1 = 1", "size": 36 },
        { "id": "rootsQF", "op": "write", "x": 100, "y": 490, "text": "x = (5 ± 1)/2 = 3 or 2", "size": 40, "color": "blue" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Switch to factoring",
      "say": "That works, but factoring is simpler here. Erase the formula work and start fresh.",
      "ops": [
        { "id": "eraseQF", "op": "erase", "ids": ["introQF", "abc", "qf", "disc", "rootsQF"] },
        { "id": "switch", "op": "write", "x": 100, "y": 230, "text": "Simpler method: factor the quadratic.", "size": 40, "color": "green" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Factor the quadratic",
      "say": "Find two numbers with product 6 and sum −5: they are −2 and −3.",
      "ops": [
        { "id": "factorHint", "op": "write", "x": 100, "y": 300, "text": "Product 6, sum −5:  −2 and −3", "size": 36 },
        { "id": "factored", "op": "write", "x": 100, "y": 370, "text": "x² − 5x + 6 = (x − 2)(x − 3)", "size": 44 }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Set each factor to zero",
      "say": "A product is zero only when one of its factors is zero.",
      "ops": [
        { "id": "zeroPrinciple", "op": "write", "x": 100, "y": 470, "text": "Set each factor equal to zero:", "size": 36 },
        { "id": "factorEqs", "op": "write", "x": 100, "y": 530, "text": "x − 2 = 0   or   x − 3 = 0", "size": 40 }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "State the solutions",
      "say": "Solving each linear equation gives x = 2 or x = 3.",
      "ops": [
        { "id": "solutions", "op": "write", "x": 100, "y": 630, "text": "x = 2   or   x = 3", "size": 52, "color": "blue" },
        { "id": "check", "op": "write", "x": 100, "y": 720, "text": "Check: both values make x² − 5x + 6 = 0.", "size": 34, "color": "gray" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "title": "Why the Pythagorean Theorem Works",
  "lang": "en",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "The theorem",
      "say": "For a right triangle with legs a, b and hypotenuse c, a² + b² = c². Let's see why.",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "write", "id": "title", "x": 800, "y": 60, "text": "Why does a² + b² = c²?", "size": 56, "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "theorem", "x": 800, "y": 150, "text": "a² + b² = c²", "size": 44, "anchor": "middle", "color": "blue" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Draw the triangle",
      "say": "Start with a right triangle. The two shorter sides are a and b, the longest side is c.",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "line", "id": "tri_ab", "x1": 300, "y1": 700, "x2": 300, "y2": 500, "color": "ink", "width": 5 },
        { "op": "line", "id": "tri_bc", "x1": 300, "y1": 700, "x2": 500, "y2": 700, "color": "ink", "width": 5 },
        { "op": "line", "id": "tri_ac", "x1": 300, "y1": 500, "x2": 500, "y2": 700, "color": "ink", "width": 5 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "label_a", "x": 270, "y": 580, "text": "a", "size": 36, "color": "blue", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "label_b", "x": 400, "y": 720, "text": "b", "size": 36, "color": "blue", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "label_c", "x": 420, "y": 570, "text": "c", "size": 36, "color": "red", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "rect", "id": "right_angle", "x": 300, "y": 680, "w": 20, "h": 20, "color": "gray", "width": 2 }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Square on side a",
      "say": "Build a square on side a. Its area is a².",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "rect", "id": "sq_a", "x": 100, "y": 500, "w": 200, "h": 200, "color": "blue", "width": 4, "fill": "blue" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "area_a", "x": 200, "y": 590, "text": "a²", "size": 40, "color": "blue", "anchor": "middle" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Square on side b",
      "say": "Build a square on side b. Its area is b².",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "rect", "id": "sq_b", "x": 300, "y": 700, "w": 200, "h": 200, "color": "green", "width": 4, "fill": "green" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "area_b", "x": 400, "y": 790, "text": "b²", "size": 40, "color": "green", "anchor": "middle" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Square on hypotenuse c",
      "say": "Build a square on the hypotenuse. Its area is c².",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "rect", "id": "sq_c", "x": 500, "y": 500, "w": 282, "h": 282, "color": "red", "width": 4, "fill": "red" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "area_c", "x": 640, "y": 630, "text": "c²", "size": 40, "color": "red", "anchor": "middle" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rearrange the pieces",
      "say": "If we rearrange the same four triangles inside a big square, the uncovered area equals c².",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "rect", "id": "big_square", "x": 1000, "y": 400, "w": 400, "h": 400, "color": "ink", "width": 4 },
        { "op": "line", "id": "rearrange1", "x1": 1000, "y1": 400, "x2": 1200, "y2": 500, "color": "gray", "width": 3, "dash": true },
        { "op": "line", "id": "rearrange2", "x1": 1400, "y1": 400, "x2": 1200, "y2": 500, "color": "gray", "width": 3, "dash": true },
        { "op": "write", "id": "rearrange_label", "x": 1200, "y": 580, "text": "c²", "size": 36, "color": "red", "anchor": "middle" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Conclusion",
      "say": "The areas match: a² + b² = c². That's why the Pythagorean theorem works.",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "write", "id": "conclusion", "x": 800, "y": 820, "text": "a² + b² = c²", "size": 48, "color": "blue", "anchor": "middle", "underline": true }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
